{"c": null, "r": "I'm designing a custom banking module with a custom exception for insufficient funds, a Bank class that manages accounts with proper validation for deposits and withdrawals, and checking validation order like ensuring the amount is positive before accessing accounts.

Writing validation logic... For `open_account`, I should validate the initial amount is non-negative before checking for duplicates, though the order doesn't matter for the tests. Dict lookups with string keys won't cause unhashable type errors, so that's fine. The test for non-positive amounts confirms that deposit operations with zero or negative values raise ValueError before mutating the balance, and unknown accounts correctly raise KeyError. I'll add an `__repr__` method and write out the module using the default_bank pattern.
", "t": [["write_file", "{"path":"D:\\Projects\\local_ai\\strata-lab\\runs\\work\\hermes\\bank-1794053343\\bank.py","content":"\"\"\"Account helpers. Balances are integer cents.\"\"\"\n\n\nclass InsufficientFunds(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when a withdrawal or transfer exceeds the source balance.\"\"\"\n\n\nclass Bank:\n    \"\"\"A bank holding its own accounts; two instances never share accounts.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._accounts = {}\n\n    def open_account(self, name, initial=0):\n        if initial < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"initial must be >= 0\")\n        if name in self._accounts:\n            raise ValueError(\"account exists: \" + name)\n        self._accounts[name] = initial\n\n    def deposit(self, name, amount):\n        self._require_amount(amount)\n        self._require_account(name)\n        self._accounts[name] += amount\n\n    def withdraw(self, name, amount):\n        self._require_amount(amount)\n        balance = self._require_account(name)\n        if balance < amount:\n            raise InsufficientFunds(\n                \"account %r has %d, cannot withdraw %d\" % (name, balance, amount)\n            )\n        self._accounts[name] = balance - amount\n\n    def balance(self, name):\n        return self._accounts[name]\n\n    def transfer(self, src, dst, amount):\n        self._require_amount(amount)\n        if src == dst:\n            raise ValueError(\"cannot transfer to the same account: \" + src)\n        src_balance = self._require_account(src)\n        self._require_account(dst)\n        if src_balance < amount:\n            raise InsufficientFunds(\n                \"account %r has %d, cannot transfer %d\" % (src, src_balance, amount)\n            )\n        self._accounts[src] = src_balance - amount\n        self._accounts[dst] += amount\n\n    def _require_amount(self, amount):\n        if amount <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"amount must be > 0\")\n\n    def _require_account(self, name):\n        try:\n            return self._accounts[name]\n        except KeyError:\n            raise KeyError(\"unknown account: \" + name)\n\n\ndefault_bank = Bank()\n\n\ndef open_account(name, initial=0):\n    return default_bank.open_account(name, initial)\n\n\ndef deposit(name, amount):\n    return default_bank.deposit(name, amount)\n\n\ndef withdraw(name, amount):\n    return default_bank.withdraw(name, amount)\n\n\ndef balance(name):\n    return default_bank.balance(name)\n\n\ndef transfer(src, dst, amount):\n    return default_bank.transfer(src, dst, amount)\n"}"]]}

